// Title: Potential CommandLine Path Traversal Via Cmd.EXE
// ID: 087790e3-3287-436c-bccf-cbd0184a7db1
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: xknow @xknow_infosec, Tim Shelton
// Date: 2020-06-11
// Tags: attack.execution, attack.t1059.003
// Description: Detects potential path traversal attempt via cmd.exe. Could indicate possible command/argument confusion/hijacking
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where (((((process.parent.command_line like "*_/c*" or process.parent.command_line like "*_/k*" or process.parent.command_line like "*_/r*")) or ((process.command_line like "*_/c*" or process.command_line like "*_/k*" or process.command_line like "*_/r*"))) and ((process.parent.executable endswith "\\cmd.exe") or (process.executable endswith "\\cmd.exe") or (process.pe.original_file_name == "cmd.exe")) and ((process.parent.command_line == "/../../") or (process.command_line like "*_/../../*"))) and not ((process.command_line like "*_\\Tasktop\\keycloak\\bin\\/../../jre\\bin\\java*")))
